# AGENTS.md template

> This is a starter template. Replace the bracketed placeholders, delete sections that do not apply, and keep the total length under 100 lines (often under 60). Every rule should trace to a real failure or a hard constraint. If you cannot defend a line, delete it.

```markdown
# Agent guide

## Build and test
- Build: `[exact command]`
- Run tests: `[exact command]`
- Run a single test: `[exact command]`
- Lint: `[exact command]`
- Typecheck: `[exact command]`
- Format: `[exact command]`

## Hard constraints
- Do not edit or remove tests. It is unacceptable to remove or skip a test because the work is harder than expected.
- Do not edit lint configuration to make CI pass.
- Do not modify files in `[path/to/legacy]` without asking the user.
- Do not run database migrations. Ask the user to run them.
- Do not commit secrets. Use `[env var pattern]` for credentials.
- [Project-specific hard constraints, one per line, each tracing to a real past failure]

## Layer rules
- Code can only depend "forward" through layers: `[Types] -> [Config] -> [Repo] -> [Service] -> [Runtime] -> [UI]`.
- Cross-cutting concerns (auth, logging, telemetry, feature flags) enter through `Providers/` only.
- Custom lint enforces this. See `docs/architecture/dependency-rules.md`.

## Conventions
- Logging: use the project logger. No `console.log` or `print` in non-test code.
- Errors: never silently swallow. Log or re-throw.
- HTTP: use the project HTTP client. Never raw `fetch` or `requests`.
- Time: use the project clock abstraction.
- IDs: `snake_case` in storage, `camelCase` in API responses.

## When you are stuck
- Read `docs/design-docs/index.md` for architectural decisions.
- Read `docs/exec-plans/active/` for in-flight work.
- Read `docs/QUALITY_SCORE.md` for known gaps in each domain.
- Search the project utility package before writing a new helper. New helpers go in the utility package, not inline.

## Session startup ritual (long-running work only)
1. `pwd`
2. Read `progress.md`
3. Read `feature_list.json`
4. `git log --oneline -20`
5. `./init.sh`
6. Run a basic smoke test
7. Only then start new work.

## Pointers
- Architecture map: `ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Design decisions: `docs/design-docs/`
- Active execution plans: `docs/exec-plans/active/`
- Vendored library docs: `docs/references/`
- Product specs: `docs/product-specs/`
- Quality grades per domain: `docs/QUALITY_SCORE.md`
```

## Common mistakes to avoid

- Do not auto-generate this file. The ETH Zurich study found LLM-generated agentfiles actively hurt resolution rates.
- Do not include codebase overviews or directory listings. Agents discover structure on their own.
- Do not include rules that nobody enforces.
- Do not write tutorials. The agent is not learning the codebase from scratch.
- Do not pad with prose. Every line competes for attention.

## How to grow it

- When the agent makes a new kind of mistake, add the line that prevents it.
- When a line stops being needed (a more capable model handles the case, or the rule is now mechanically enforced by a lint), remove it.
- When a section grows past 10 lines, consider whether it should move to a doc that AGENTS.md points to.
- Re-review the file every couple of months. Cut anything that no longer earns its place.
